{
  name = "robot-bringup";
  description = "Patterns for bringing up a complete ROS2 robot stack on the onboard computer: systemd services for launch, ordered startup with health checks, layered launch-file composition, udev rules for deterministic device naming, watchdog monitoring, log rotation, and graceful shutdown. Use when configuring a robot to start ROS2 nodes on boot, writing systemd units that source a workspace, composing full-stack launch files, fixing boot-time race conditions, or setting up multi-machine ROS2 networking. Covers ROS2 Humble and Jazzy (recommended) on Ubuntu 22.04/24.04; Iron is EOL.";
}
